# The anchors of the identity system, recomputed and compared to what they
# were pinned at.
#
# Every other cross-implementation test in this suite proves that the two
# implementations agree with each other. None of them can notice that the two
# now agree on something else — a coordinated change moves both legs, the diff
# still passes, and every identity in the system has quietly become a different
# identity. That is the failure this test exists for. It is also why the
# re-mint tool refuses to update these values on its own: a tripwire that
# resets itself is furniture.
#
# When this test fails after a deliberate identity change, read the report,
# confirm each move is the one you meant, and run:
#   python3 tools/remint/remint.py sentinels --accept
# REQUIRES: uv

# RUN: %python %zkc-remint sentinels | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: 12/12 anchors hold
